 "result": "**Result:** 24 failed, 462 passed, 1 skipped, 1 error (the error is in setup of `test_stream_keeps_session`, which also fails).\n\n**Main root cause:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374` (`persist_session`) calls `response.set_cookie(..., partitioned=partitioned, ...)`. The installed Werkzeug's `Response.set_cookie()` doesn't accept a `partitioned` keyword (added in newer Werkzeug), so it raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The same unsupported argument is passed to `delete_cookie`. Any test that saves a session cookie fails, which accounts for about 20 of the 24 failures. These include the session tests in `test_basic.py`, `test_extended_flashing`, `test_flash_signal`, `test_standard_context`, `test_copy_context_thread`, the `test_testing.py` session tests, and `test_stream_keeps_session`.\n\nThis looks like a Werkzeug version mismatch: the code requires a newer Werkzeug than the one installed.\n\n**Other failures (likely separate causes, not fully diagnosed):**\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`: `RuntimeError`, probably a missing async dependency.\n- `test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`: a `pytest.Pytest...` error, probably a pytest-version issue.\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name`: `AssertionError`.\n- `test_request.py::test_limit_config`: `assert None...`, likely a config attribute that the installed Werkzeug lacks.\n\nI didn't look at these four in detail, and I changed nothing.",
